    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's more than just a \"coping method.\" it's the reality. there is no \"unlearning\" how much rent costs or how much debt i've built up just to stay afloat. it feels like we're just taught to accept this slow decay until we're too exhausted to even care anymore. when the math is just fundamentally broken, it feels like the only way to actually stop the drain is to just... stop participating entirely. like, why keep playing a game that was rigged from the start?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
